   "content": [
      {
         "id": "da6b50bc-f1c3-402a-bffe-5c96b91a0b95",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "nerd",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nWhen we studied addition, we saw that the complement of 10 helps us calculate. And addition is not the only operation where it is useful.\n\nIn this class, we are going to learn how to use the complement to do subtraction.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "a3c9ade2-8d8a-4578-bf8a-56495f76d739",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "a3c9ade2-8d8a-4578-bf8a-56495f76d739",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Complement\n\nTo begin, let us remember what the complement of 10 is. The complement of 10 is how much we need to add to a number to reach 10.\n\nFor example, in the figure below we can see that the complement of 6 is 4, because 6 + 4 = 10.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 632 56\" width=\"100%\" style=\"max-width:632px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six light blue squares followed by four light yellow squares\"><title>Six light blue squares and four light yellow squares, ten in all</title><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"256\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"448\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"512\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"576\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 1</b>: The number 6 (light blue) and its complement 4 (light yellow); together they fill the ten squares.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "8c63a4e2-56c7-4d84-9d95-c683a4ad84b0",
         "prev": "da6b50bc-f1c3-402a-bffe-5c96b91a0b95",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "8c63a4e2-56c7-4d84-9d95-c683a4ad84b0",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "nerd",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Splitting in Orders\n\nBefore we subtract, we also need to remember another characteristic of numbers: every number can be split into orders.\n\nThe number 12, for example, is made of one ten and two units, and it can be written as:\n\n12 = 10 + 2\n\nHere, 10 is the value of the tens order, and 2 is the value of the units order.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "fd4fe060-1e86-4c87-a552-984d857b26a2",
         "prev": "a3c9ade2-8d8a-4578-bf8a-56495f76d739",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "fd4fe060-1e86-4c87-a552-984d857b26a2",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Everything Together\n\nNow we are going to use everything we have remembered to calculate 12 − 7. This means that, from the 12 squares below, we want to remove 7.\n\nWe will represent the removal by changing the color of the squares from light blue to light yellow.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 56\" width=\"100%\" style=\"max-width:760px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Twelve light blue squares\"><title>Twelve light blue squares representing the number 12</title><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"256\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"448\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"512\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"576\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"640\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"704\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 2</b>: The 12 squares of the number 12, before the subtraction.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "105a9799-5da8-45a4-81a5-b2248a2525a6",
         "prev": "8c63a4e2-56c7-4d84-9d95-c683a4ad84b0",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "105a9799-5da8-45a4-81a5-b2248a2525a6",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Evaluating the Units\n\nThe units digit of 12 is 2, and 2 is smaller than 7. This means we cannot subtract 7 from the 2 units alone.\n\nSo we reorganize the numbers using the orders we remembered:\n\n12 − 7 =\n(2 + 10) − 7 =\n2 + (10 − 7)\n\nIn the figure, the seven faded light yellow squares are the 7 we remove from the ten. The three light yellow squares that remain are the complement of 7 to 10. The two light blue squares are the units of 12.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 56\" width=\"100%\" style=\"max-width:760px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Seven faded light yellow squares, three light yellow squares and two light blue squares\"><title>Seven faded light yellow squares, three light yellow squares and two light blue squares</title><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"256\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"448\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"512\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"576\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"640\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"704\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 3</b>: Seven faded light yellow squares (the 7 removed), three light yellow squares (the complement) and two light blue squares (the units).</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "fd64c19f-90a5-48cc-8d89-39ed7f876319",
         "prev": "fd4fe060-1e86-4c87-a552-984d857b26a2",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "fd64c19f-90a5-48cc-8d89-39ed7f876319",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1adedc53-a246-49d1-aa42-cee0fd3aa553",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Result\n\nNow we can finish the calculation:\n\n10 − 7 = 3\n2 + 3 = 5\n\nSo, 12 − 7 = 5. In the figure below, the seven faded light yellow squares are the 7 we removed, and the five light blue squares are the result. Together they still show the 12 we started with.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 56\" width=\"100%\" style=\"max-width:760px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Seven faded light yellow squares and five light blue squares\"><title>Seven faded light yellow squares and five light blue squares representing the calculation 12 minus 7 equals 5</title><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"256\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" fill-opacity=\"0.3\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"448\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"512\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"576\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"640\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"704\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 4</b>: Seven faded light yellow squares (the 7 removed) and five light blue squares (the result).</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "054e630a-ef4a-46be-b3ae-2697dafd9a7b",
